            <ArticleTitle>Perforation of jejunal duplication lined with ectopic gastric mucosa.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>649-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Alimentary tract duplications are rare congenital anomalies that occasionally contain ectopic gastric mucosa that secretes acid peptic juice and can cause pain, ulceration, bleeding and rarely perforation. We report a case of a 2-year-old girl who developed perforation of a jejunal duplication lined with ectopic gastric mucosa who was managed surgically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
